nterpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    name: error_analysis\n    claim: \"C5\"\n    description: >\n      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    name: reliability_test\n    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n    description: >\n      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-4.1) = 360 episodes. Local models added when plan_003 GPU available.\n      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n      [2026-05-20] API portion: 330/360 episodes complete (28/30 clauses),\n      judgments pending.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    name: realism_validation\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n 